<title>POLAND: ComputerLand surges on foreign demand.</title>
<headline>ComputerLand surges on foreign demand.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish software firm ComputerLand SA surged 9.9 percent in active trade to 78 zlotys as foreign investors continued their blue-chip buying that has sent the main market to five straight 33-month highs.</p>
<p>&quot;ComputerLand has shown a strong earnings growth dynamic... and its obtaining of a strategic investor helps,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>The firm announced last week that Vanstar Corporation had bought 7.52 percent of ComputerLand shares, gaining the same percentage of shareholder votes.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
